      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the perimeter of the triangle. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a triangle with sides \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nP = a + b + c\n\\]\n\nGiven the side lengths of the triangle are \\( 6.1 \\) cm, \\( 8.2 \\) cm, and \\( 9.7 \\) cm, we can calculate the perimeter as follows:\n\n\\[\nP = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\n\\[\nP = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7 = 24.0 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nSince the square and the triangle have equal perimeters, the perimeter of the square is also \\( 24.0 \\) cm. Let the side length of the square be \\( s \\). The perimeter of the square is given by:\n\n\\[\n4s = 24.0\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( s \\):\n\n\\[\ns = \\frac{24.0}{4} = 6.0 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the side length of the square, we can find its area. The area \\( A \\) of a square with side length \\( s \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nA = s^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the side length \\( s = 6.0 \\) cm:\n\n\\[\nA = 6.0^2 = 36.0 \\text{ square centimeters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36.0}\n\\]",
